suppository versus placebo prior to vacuum aspiration. Both arms receive the same surgical termination method (vacuum 
aspiration). The trial evaluates cervical preparation, not a comparison of different surgical abortion methods, so it 
falls outside the review objective.

- **Study 5 (INCLUDE, high confidence):** 420 women were randomly assigned to D&C or vacuum aspiration for 
first-trimester abortion. It is an RCT explicitly comparing two different surgical techniques, matching the review’s 
eligibility criteria perfectly.

- **Study 6 (INCLUDE, high confidence):** Eighty-four women were randomised to manual versus electric vacuum aspiration 
for first-trimester elective abortion (<10 weeks). It is an RCT comparing two different surgical aspiration methods and 
