- **Study 8 (EXCLUDE, medium confidence):** Forty-seven women underwent vacuum aspiration or classical D&C. However, the
abstract does not mention randomisation, and the description suggests a non-randomised comparative or cohort design. 
Because the protocol requires RCTs and there is no evidence of random allocation, the study was excluded at 
title/abstract screening, though the limited abstract information warrants medium rather than high confidence.

- **Study 9 (EXCLUDE, high confidence):** Three hundred subjects were randomly assigned to metal or flexible plastic 
cannulae for vacuum aspiration. While it is an RCT, it compares equipment variants within the same surgical method 
rather than comparing different surgical methods (e.g., D&C vs VA or MVA vs EVA). Therefore it does not satisfy the 
review objective.

- **Study 10 (INCLUDE, high confidence):** One hundred and fourteen women were enrolled in a randomised trial comparing 
manual vacuum aspiration with electric vacuum curettage for first-trimester abortion. It is an RCT comparing two 
surgical methods and is eligible.

